{"ts": "2026-09-26T09:45:00+00:00", "module": "B2-C crisis-derisk", "window": "2019-08-01..2026-09-26 BTCUSDT 1H (Bitget perp)", "change": "v0 as pre-declared in docs/spec-B2-crisis-derisk.md section 4 (C1 r_24h<=-10%; C2 rv_24h>=2x 90d median & r_24h<0; C3 any listed stablecoin daily close<=0.97; C4 crisis-topic share>=365d 90th pct & r_24h<0; cooldown 7d; re-entry r_24h>0)", "result": {"module": {"return": 0.045, "sharpe": 0.16, "max_dd": -0.613, "calmar": 0.01, "time_in_market": 0.28}, "buy_hold": {"return": 7.334, "sharpe": 0.79, "max_dd": -0.772, "calmar": 0.45}, "ma200": {"return": 6.202, "sharpe": 0.82, "max_dd": -0.652, "calmar": 0.49}, "voltarget40": {"return": 4.159, "sharpe": 0.74, "max_dd": -0.647, "calmar": 0.40}, "episodes": 77, "false_alarms": 49, "events_triggered": "9/9"}, "verdict": "FAIL all three spec criteria", "note": "implementation error found after the run: C3 stayed on for 13,137 hours because UST (USTC) trades near 0 after May 2022; the rule read 'any coin <= 0.97' literally. Fixed in the next entry as a definition fix, not a threshold change."}
{"ts": "2026-09-26T09:50:00+00:00", "module": "B2-C crisis-derisk", "window": "same", "change": "v0.1 definition fix: C3 = a FRESH break (some coin closes <= 0.97 today and closed >= 0.99 seven days earlier), so a dead coin cannot keep the rule on. Thresholds unchanged. Also added the rule-alone / leave-one-out ablation to metrics.json as diagnostics.", "result": {"module": {"return": 0.376, "sharpe": 0.30, "max_dd": -0.612, "calmar": 0.07, "time_in_market": 0.40, "episodes": 90, "false_alarms": 55, "false_alarm_rate": 0.61, "fa_mean_missed": 0.078, "hit_mean_avoided": -0.053, "events_triggered": "9/9"}, "module_plus_ma200": {"return": 0.286, "max_dd": -0.552, "calmar": 0.06, "time_in_market": 0.25}, "funding_sens_0.01pct_8h": {"module_return": 0.002, "buy_hold_return": 2.805}, "rule_hours_true": {"C1": 364, "C2": 2585, "C3": 624, "C4": 4189}, "episodes_first_rule": {"C1": 8, "C2": 39, "C3": 5, "C4": 38}}, "ablation_diagnostic": "C1 only: ret +504%, maxDD -69.5%, calmar 0.41, 28 episodes / 16 false alarms, 7/9 events; C3 only (pre-fix numbers superseded); C2 only and C4 only each ~70 episodes with >50% false alarms; no single rule or subset beats the 200-day MA on Calmar", "verdict": "FAIL all three spec criteria. Diagnosis: C2 (2x median) fires in ~4% of hours (the 90th pct of the ratio is 1.86, 98th is 3.08) and C4 fires by construction ~10% of days; both are far too frequent for a crisis rule. The 7-day cooldown + 'first positive r_24h' re-entry re-enters inside bear trends (2021-11..2022-11) so max DD is barely reduced. Any threshold change from here is a v1 trial: tune on dev events E1-E5 only, run holdout E6-E9 once."}
{"ts": "2026-09-26T10:40:00+00:00", "module": "B2-C crisis-derisk", "window": "dev 2019-08-01..2022-12-31 (E1-E5) for selection; holdout 2023-01-01..2026-09-26 (E6-E9) once", "change": "v1.0 grid (16 configs): C1, C3 always on; C2 off | 3x; C4 off | q95 for 2 consecutive days; re-entry after the 7d cooldown 'recover' (open > exit price) | 'ma20' (daily close > 20d MA); base 1 | 200d MA. Selection = module Calmar over its base minus the base's Calmar.", "result": {"dev_best": {"config": "C2 off, C4 off, recover, base 1", "module": {"return": 0.604, "max_dd": -0.565, "calmar": 0.26}, "base_calmar": 0.20, "increment": 0.06, "episodes": 14, "false_alarms": 9}, "dev_with_ma200_base": "every configuration has a NEGATIVE increment over the 200d MA (-0.11 .. -0.36)", "holdout_chosen": {"return": 0.023, "max_dd": -0.594, "calmar": 0.01, "buy_hold_return": 4.078, "ma200_calmar": 1.19, "episodes": 12, "false_alarms": 7}}, "verdict": "FAIL", "note": "C3 fresh-break was firing on BUSD/FRAX/TUSD wind-downs (BUSD 15 break-days) - not crises. Fixed in v1.1 as a definition change (MAJOR_STABLES = USDT USDC DAI USDe UST). Holdout was therefore looked at once with the noisy C3."}
{"ts": "2026-09-26T10:55:00+00:00", "module": "B2-C crisis-derisk", "window": "same dev/holdout", "change": "v1.1: C3 on MAJOR_STABLES only; new rule C5 (Deribit DVOL hourly close >= 1.25x trailing-30d median = 95th pct of the ratio, with r_24h < 0; DVOL exists from 2021-03-24, free public API) added to the grid (32 configs). SECOND look at the holdout (disclosed).", "result": {"dev_best": {"config": "C2 off, C4 off, C5 off, recover, base 1", "increment": 0.06}, "c5_effect_on_dev": "none: C1/C3 already fire at the hours C5 fires, or the module is already out", "holdout_chosen": {"return": 0.272, "max_dd": -0.594, "calmar": 0.11, "sharpe": 0.36, "time_in_market": 0.67, "episodes": 4, "false_alarms": 4, "events_hit": "3/4"}, "holdout_refs": {"buy_hold": {"return": 4.078, "max_dd": -0.538, "calmar": 1.01}, "ma200": {"return": 2.569, "max_dd": -0.340, "calmar": 1.19}, "voltarget40": {"return": 3.207, "max_dd": -0.529, "calmar": 0.89}}}, "verdict": "FAIL. Root cause of the holdout loss: the 'recover' re-entry keeps the module out from the 2022-05 Terra exit (~33k) until BTC recovers that level in 2024-02, i.e. it misses 2023-24 entirely; it only looked good on dev because staying out of the 2022 bear is right in-sample. 'ma20' re-enters into every bounce. Detection itself is fine (lead-time table, REPORT 7a): C2 at 2x fires before or within a day of 8 of 9 events with 8-48% still to fall; the cost is the false alarms between events.", "next": "stop tuning triggers. Either (a) make the 200d MA the strategy and test the crisis rules only as an overlay INSIDE uptrends with a fixed short cooldown (3d) and MA re-entry, judged on drawdown-in-uptrend; or (b) move on to the F (fragility) and A (accumulate) layers and use DVOL there as a slow input."}
